From: Vlastimil Babka <vbabka@suse.cz>
Subject: kabi: struct user_struct perf_mlock kabi fixup
Patch-mainline: Never, kABI workaround
References: CVE-2026-93243 bsc#1282687

The backport of commit 78436f3882fb ("perf: Track the perf mlock gift
separately") added new perf_mlock field to user_struct. Move it as last and
hide it from genksyms. Modules are not allocating this struct directly so the
larger size should not be an issue.

Signed-off-by: Vlastimil Babka <vbabka@suse.cz>
Reviewed-by: Jan Kara <jack@suse.cz>
---
 include/linux/sched/user.h |    9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/include/linux/sched/user.h
+++ b/include/linux/sched/user.h
@@ -28,15 +28,18 @@ struct user_struct {
 	defined(CONFIG_SECRETMEM)
 	atomic_long_t locked_vm;	/* pinned pages charged to RLIMIT_MEMLOCK */
 #endif
-#ifdef CONFIG_PERF_EVENTS
-	atomic_long_t perf_mlock;	/* perf buffer pages within perf_event_mlock_kb */
-#endif
 #ifdef CONFIG_WATCH_QUEUE
 	atomic_t nr_watches;	/* The number of watches this user currently has */
 #endif
 
 	/* Miscellaneous per-user rate limit */
 	struct ratelimit_state ratelimit;
+
+#ifndef __GENKSYMS__
+#ifdef CONFIG_PERF_EVENTS
+	atomic_long_t perf_mlock;	/* perf buffer pages within perf_event_mlock_kb */
+#endif
+#endif
 };
 
 extern int uids_sysfs_init(void);
